title: Housing
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/housing.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and housing_timer <= 0
on-arrival: housing_timer = 5; month_actions += 1

= Housing

One in three British households rents from a council. [+ environment_secretary +] at the Environment department wants to change that.

- @right_to_buy: Give council tenants the right to buy.
- @bigger_discounts: Increase the right-to-buy discounts.
- @cut_building: Cut council house building.
- @mortgage_relief: Protect mortgage interest relief.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@right_to_buy
view-if: right_to_buy_progress = 0
subtitle: +1 budget. A lasting boost among skilled and working-class voters.
on-arrival: right_to_buy_progress += 1; budget += 1; c2_con += 2*(1-dissent); de_con += 2*(1-dissent); policy_right_to_buy = 1

The Housing Act gives every council tenant of three years' standing the right to buy their home at a discount of up to 50%. Labour councils try to drag their feet; the law says they can't.

@bigger_discounts
view-if: right_to_buy_progress >= 1 and right_to_buy_progress < 4
subtitle: Speeds up sales.
on-arrival: right_to_buy_progress += 1; c2_con += 2*(1-dissent); de_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent += 1

Larger discounts and easier mortgages for tenants. The queue at the town hall grows longer.

@cut_building
subtitle: +1 budget.
on-arrival: budget += 1; de_con -= 1; de_lab += 1; wet_dissent += 2

Council house building falls to its lowest level since the war. Waiting lists grow.

@mortgage_relief
subtitle: -1 budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; c1_con += 2*(1-dissent); c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); dry_dissent += 2

Mortgage interest relief is safe. The Treasury points out that it's a subsidy to the middle classes; Number 10 points out who votes.
